  actor: jgstern_agent  # bbbc
  clock: 4  # bbbc
  nonce: bbbc  # bbbc
  message: "Done in PR #1956 (caa332e01c). Root cause: linkers/js_module.py _is_relative_import accepted ./ and ../ prefixes only, so '.' and '..' took the bare-specifier route and became npm package nodes named '.' / '..'. Fix: exactly '.' and '..' are relative; a relative import naming a directory with a package.json loads its entry (js_package_entry.package_entry, Node's LOAD_AS_DIRECTORY), else the index. CLOSURE EVIDENCE, production hypergumbo survey on merged dev: apollo-server has no package node named '.' or '..' (was 5 edges to them); packages/server/src/__tests__/logger.test.ts:1 import from '..' -> packages/server/src/index.ts file node; packages/integration-testsuite/src/apolloServerTests.ts:43 '.' -> its src/index.ts. Branch A/B (same code) on the other repos: nuclear 25 package edges -> index.ts files, pm2 5 removed with no in-tree target (examples/ has no manifest or index), knex 4 added ('../../../..' -> the root package.json main knex.js); every edge read."  # bbbc
